    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\n\nWith multicursors placed, an Insert-mode mapping that edits the buffer via API (`nvim_put()`, `nvim_buf_set_text()`, `vim.snippet.expand()`, …) is mirrored at the other cursors while in Insert mode, but the edit is dropped when Insert mode ends. Only literally typed keys survive the final replay, so the text the user just saw at the other cursors disappears on `<Esc>`.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n```\n$ cat minimal.lua\nvim.keymap.set('i', '<C-j>', function() vim.api.nvim_put({ 'X' }, 'c', false, true) end)\n\n$ nvim --clean -u minimal.lua \n```\n\nBuffer:\n\n```\nfoo\nbar\n```\n\nType `QjQA<C-j><Esc>`.\n\nAfter `<C-j>` (still in Insert mode) both lines show `fooX` / `barX`. After `<Esc>`:\n\n```\nfoo\nbarX\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n```\nfooX\nbarX\n```\n\nThe committed result should match what was mirrored live at the other cursors (or the live mirroring should not show an edit that will not be replayed).\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1782+gdce927183c\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nmacOS (Darwin 27.0.0),\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nWezTerm 20260901-002820-4fbd6b8e\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\ndownload from repo",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
